From upstream vLLM PR #58560 (merged Oct 5 2026 as 49e0f4797853da0d1da7fdfe794f327fb5d5843d, after our pin), author bluemelov1, Apache-2.0:
"[Bugfix][DSv4.1] Keep the compressor ring out of the null block" (fixes #57156).
Dummy / warmup / capture batches have zeroed block tables, so the compressor ring wrote fp32 state rows into
block 0, the null block every KV group shares; FlashInfer's SM120 sparse MLA gathers block 0 for masked slots and
0 x NaN = NaN. Measured on our G0 (Oct 8): 3-layer truncated V4.1 on GB10 = NaN logits from layer 0's attention,
1-layer (no compressor) = finite. Carried unchanged until our pin moves past 49e0f479.

